   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to mandatory quality review of certified public accountants",
    "basePrintNo": "S6026",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6026-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7410, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6026              REVISED MEMO 05/11/2017\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nmandatory quality review of certified public accountants\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to remove the exemption of mandatory\nquality review, based on regulations promulgated by the department as\na condition of renewal of registration, for sole proprietorship firms\nand firms with two or fewer accounting professionals.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph 1 of Section 7410 of the Education Law to\nremove the exemption of mandatory quality review, based on regulations\npromulgated by the department as a condition of renewal of\nregistration, for sole proprietorship firms and firms with two or\nfewer accounting professionals.\n\nThe first section also strikes paragraph 2 of Section 7410 of the\nEducation Law to remove the exemption of mandatory quality review,\nbased on regulations promulgated by the department as a condition of\nrenewal of registration, for sole proprietorship firms and firms with\ntwo or fewer accounting professionals.\n\nSection 2 sets an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCurrently, sole proprietorship firms and firms with two or fewer\naccounting professionals are not required to undergo mandatory quality\nreview as a condition of renewal of registration. New York is the only\nstate that provides this exemption for sole and smaller firms.  All\nfirms, regardless of size, that perform audit and attest services,\nshould be required to undergo mandatory quality review. Mandatory\nquality review/peer review ensures adequate quality-control. It\nensures that CPA firms follow best practices. This would ensure that\npublic interest is protected and would ensure the dependability of\ninformation used for guidance in financial transactions.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
